module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpChartCover.Cartier
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.BlowupFormsChartPoleBound
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealActionSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealSheafSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.PullbackVanishingOpenImmersion

/-!
# The pole bound of Stacks 0G5G

In the situation of `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.BlowupDifferentialFormsComparison` —
a ring `R`, `S = Spec(R)`, the coordinate closed immersion `Z = 𝐀^m_S ⟶ 𝐀^{m+n}_S = X`, the
blowup `b : L ⟶ X` of `X` along `Z` and its exceptional divisor `E ⊆ L` — the first canonical
map of [Stacks, Tag 0G5G] is `φ : b^*Ω^a_{X/S} ⟶ Ω^a_{L/S}`
(`Stacks.DeRham.blowupFormsPullbackMap`), a monomorphism by
`Stacks.DeRham.mono_blowupFormsPullbackMap`.

**This file proves the pole bound**

`ℐ_{(n-1)E} · Ω^a_{L/S} ⊆ b^*Ω^a_{X/S}`,

which is the geometric content of the second half of the source's proof: on the `i`-th standard
chart the exceptional divisor is cut out by `y_i`, and `d t_j = (d y_j - t_j d y_i) / y_i` shows
that `y_i^{n-1}` clears the pole of any `a`-fold wedge of chart differentials. Granted it,
`Stacks.Divisors.twistedRetraction` produces the second canonical map of the tag and
`Stacks.Divisors.comp_twistedRetraction` identifies the composite; that is done in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.BlowupFormsTwistedComparison`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.DeRham.ExceptionalPoleBound`: the containment above, spelled as the vanishing of the
  action of the ideal sheaf of `(n-1)E` modulo the first canonical map.
* `Stacks.DeRham.coordinateChartOpen`: the image of the `i`-th standard chart, as an affine open
  of the blowup.
* `Stacks.DeRham.coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator`: the generator of the ideal of `(n-1)E`
  there, namely the `(n-1)`-st power of the pullback of `y_i`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.DeRham.ideal_coordinateExceptional_pow_coordinateChartOpen` and
  `Stacks.DeRham.coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator_eq`: on the `i`-th standard chart the ideal
  of `(n-1)E` is generated by that section, and that section is the restriction of the global
  section `Stacks.DeRham.coordinateBlowupPoleSection` of `𝒪_L`.
* `Stacks.DeRham.exceptionalPoleBound`: **the pole bound.**

## How the chart computation is assembled into the bound

`Stacks.Divisors.idealAction_comp_eq_zero` removes the sheaf tensor product from the statement:
the vanishing to be proved follows from a statement about *sections*, namely that the cokernel of
`φ` kills every section `ι(r) · s` with `r` a section of `ℐ_{(n-1)E}` and `s` a section of
`Ω^a_{L/S}` over a common open `V`, the action on such a section being multiplication by `ι(r)`
(`Stacks.Divisors.idealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection`). So neither a compatibility of the
inverse image with the tensor product nor an identification of `(b^*) ℐ_D` with the ideal sheaf
of a comap is needed.

That vanishing is local on `V` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.
app_eq_zero_of_forall_exists_le`), and the `n` standard charts cover `L`
(`Stacks.MoreMorphisms.exists_mem_range_coordinateBlowupChart`), so it may be checked on
`W = V ⊓ L_i` for a chart containing the point at hand. There the ideal of `(n-1)E` is generated
by one nonzerodivisor, so `ι(r)|_W` is a multiple of it
(`Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero`), that generator is the restriction of a
global section of `𝒪_L`, and the cokernel of `φ` kills its multiples by
`Stacks.DeRham.cokernelπ_app_smul_poleSection_eq_zero`.

## Which blowup this is

`Stacks.DeRham.coordinateBlowup` is `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`, and
`Stacks.DeRham.coordinateExceptional` is the **reducible**
`AlgebraicGeometry.exceptionalIdeal`, which is the one
`Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.ideal_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span_chartGenerator` computes. The library has
a second constant `Stacks.Blowup.exceptionalIdeal` with the same body, and two further blowup
models `Stacks.Blowup.blowUp` and `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec` with no isomorphism to
`AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`; nothing stated for those applies here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G5G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G5G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.DeRham

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (m n : ℕ)

/-- **The pole bound of [Stacks, Tag 0G5G], as a containment of subsheaves of `Ω^a_{L/S}`:**
`ℐ_{(n-1)E} · Ω^a_{L/S} ⊆ b^*Ω^a_{X/S}`.

It is spelled as the vanishing of the action `Stacks.Divisors.idealAction` of the ideal sheaf of
`(n-1)E` on `Ω^a_{L/S}` modulo the first canonical map, which for a monomorphism — and
`Stacks.DeRham.mono_blowupFormsPullbackMap` says the first canonical map is one — is exactly that
containment, and is the form `Stacks.Divisors.idealActionFactor` consumes. It is proved in
`Stacks.DeRham.exceptionalPoleBound`. -/
def ExceptionalPoleBound (a : ℕ) : Prop :=
  Stacks.Divisors.idealAction (coordinateExceptional R m n ^ (n - 1))
      (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms (coordinateBlowupToBase R m n) a) ≫
    cokernel.π (blowupFormsPullbackMap R m n a) = 0

variable (i : Fin n)

/-- The image of the `i`-th standard chart of the coordinate blowup, as an affine open of the
blowup. -/
noncomputable abbrev coordinateChartOpen : (coordinateBlowup R m n).affineOpens :=
  Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartOpen (Stacks.MoreMorphisms.coordinateIdeal R m n)
    (Stacks.MoreMorphisms.topAffineOpen R m n)
    (Stacks.MoreMorphisms.coordinateIdealSection R m n i)

/-- The generator of the ideal of `(n-1)E` on the `i`-th standard chart: the `(n-1)`-st power of
the pullback of `y_i` along the blowing-up morphism. -/
noncomputable abbrev coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator :
    Γ(coordinateBlowup R m n, (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1) :=
  Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartGenerator (Stacks.MoreMorphisms.coordinateIdeal R m n)
    (Stacks.MoreMorphisms.topAffineOpen R m n)
    (Stacks.MoreMorphisms.coordinateIdealSection R m n i) ^ (n - 1)

/-- **The image of the `i`-th standard chart is the range of the chart's open immersion.** The
`Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chart` of the development computing the exceptional ideal and the
`AlgebraicGeometry.blowupChartι` that `Stacks.DeRham.coordinateBlowupChartι` is defined from are
the same morphism. -/
theorem coe_coordinateChartOpen :
    (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1 = (coordinateBlowupChartι R m n i).opensRange := rfl

/-- **On the `i`-th standard chart the ideal of `(n-1)E` is generated by `y_i^{n-1}`.** On that
chart the exceptional ideal itself is generated by the pullback of `y_i`
(`Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.ideal_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span_chartGenerator`), and the ideal of a
power of a closed subscheme is the corresponding power of its ideal. -/
theorem ideal_coordinateExceptional_pow_coordinateChartOpen :
    (coordinateExceptional R m n ^ (n - 1)).ideal (coordinateChartOpen R m n i) =
      Ideal.span {coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator R m n i} := by
  rw [show (coordinateExceptional R m n ^ (n - 1)).ideal (coordinateChartOpen R m n i) =
      (coordinateExceptional R m n).ideal (coordinateChartOpen R m n i) ^ (n - 1) from rfl,
    Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.ideal_exceptionalIdeal_eq_span_chartGenerator,
    Ideal.span_singleton_pow]

/-- **The generator of the ideal of `(n-1)E` on the `i`-th standard chart is a
nonzerodivisor.** -/
theorem coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors :
    coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator R m n i ∈
      nonZeroDivisors Γ(coordinateBlowup R m n, (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1) :=
  pow_mem (Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors _ _ _) (n - 1)

/-- **The generator of the ideal of `(n-1)E` on the `i`-th standard chart is the restriction of a
global section of `𝒪_L`**, namely of the pullback along `b` of `y_i^{n-1}`. -/
theorem coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator_eq :
    coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator R m n i =
      (coordinateBlowup R m n).presheaf.map (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1.leTop.op
        (coordinateBlowupPoleSection R m n i) := by
  have hpole : Stacks.MoreMorphisms.coordinateSection R m n i ^ (n - 1) =
      coordinateChartPoleSection R m n i := by
    rw [coordinateChartPoleSection, map_pow]
    rfl
  change ((coordinateBlowupToAmbient R m n).appLE ⊤ (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1
      (Stacks.BlowUpChartCover.chartOpen_le _ _ _)
      (Stacks.MoreMorphisms.coordinateSection R m n i)) ^ (n - 1) = _
  rw [← map_pow, hpole]
  rfl

/-- **The cokernel of the first canonical map kills every section of `ℐ_{(n-1)E} · Ω^a_{L/S}`.**
This is the pole bound at the level of sections, and it is where the standard charts enter: the
statement is local on `V`, the `n` charts cover `L`, and on the part of `V` inside the `i`-th
chart the section of the ideal sheaf is a multiple of `y_i^{n-1}`, whose multiples the cokernel
kills by `Stacks.DeRham.cokernelπ_app_smul_poleSection_eq_zero`. -/
theorem cokernelπ_app_smul_idealSheafSection_eq_zero (a : ℕ)
    (V : (coordinateBlowup R m n).Opens)
    (r : (Stacks.Divisors.negativeTwist' (coordinateExceptional R m n ^ (n - 1))).val.obj (op V))
    (s : Γ(Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms (coordinateBlowupToBase R m n) (a : ℤ), V)) :
    (cokernel.π (blowupFormsPullbackMap R m n a)).app V
        (Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafSection (coordinateExceptional R m n ^ (n - 1)) r • s) = 0 := by
  refine Scheme.Modules.app_eq_zero_of_forall_exists_le _ _ fun y hy => ?_
  obtain ⟨i, z, hz⟩ := Stacks.MoreMorphisms.exists_mem_range_coordinateBlowupChart R m n y
  refine ⟨V ⊓ (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1, inf_le_left,
    ⟨hy, (coe_coordinateChartOpen R m n i).ge ⟨z, hz⟩⟩, ?_⟩
  rw [Scheme.Modules.map_smul]
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero
    (coordinateExceptional R m n ^ (n - 1)) (coordinateChartOpen R m n i)
    (ideal_coordinateExceptional_pow_coordinateChartOpen R m n i)
    (coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator_mem_nonZeroDivisors R m n i)
    (inf_le_right : V ⊓ (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1 ≤ (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1) _
    (Stacks.Divisors.subschemeι_app_eq_zero_of_le _ inf_le_left
      (Stacks.Divisors.subschemeι_app_idealSheafSection _ r))
  have hgen : (coordinateBlowup R m n).presheaf.map
        (homOfLE (inf_le_right :
          V ⊓ (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1 ≤ (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1)).op
        (coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator R m n i) =
      (coordinateBlowup R m n).presheaf.map (V ⊓ (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1).leTop.op
        (coordinateBlowupPoleSection R m n i) := by
    rw [coordinateChartExceptionalGenerator_eq]
    exact Stacks.Divisors.res_res _ _ _
  rw [hc, hgen, mul_smul, Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul,
    cokernelπ_app_smul_poleSection_eq_zero R m n i a
      (W := V ⊓ (coordinateChartOpen R m n i).1) inf_le_right _, smul_zero]

/-- **The pole bound of [Stacks, Tag 0G5G]:** `ℐ_{(n-1)E} · Ω^a_{L/S} ⊆ b^*Ω^a_{X/S}`.

`Stacks.Divisors.idealAction_comp_eq_zero` reduces the vanishing to the statement about sections
`Stacks.DeRham.cokernelπ_app_smul_idealSheafSection_eq_zero`: the action of the ideal sheaf on
the image of a local pure tensor `r ⊗ s` is multiplication by the image of `r` under the
inclusion `ℐ_{(n-1)E} ⟶ 𝒪_L`. -/
theorem exceptionalPoleBound (a : ℕ) : ExceptionalPoleBound R m n a :=
  Stacks.Divisors.idealAction_comp_eq_zero _ (cokernel.π (blowupFormsPullbackMap R m n a))
    fun U r s =>
      (congrArg
            (fun z => (((cokernel.π (blowupFormsPullbackMap R m n a)).val.app U).hom) z)
            (Stacks.Divisors.idealAction_val_app_toTensorSheafSection
              (coordinateExceptional R m n ^ (n - 1))
              (Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentialForms (coordinateBlowupToBase R m n) (a : ℤ))
              U r s)).trans
        (cokernelπ_app_smul_idealSheafSection_eq_zero R m n a U.unop r s)

end Stacks.DeRham

end
